The failing test is `r-unreadable-file-in-tree-is-an-error`. The issue is that when a file inside the tree cannot be opened/read, it should return exit code 2 (error), but currently the code returns 0. Looking at line 437-446 in the current implementation, when `search_directory` encounters an unreadable file, it sets `error_occurred = true` but the function itself doesn't properly propagate error status from nested calls.

The problem is in how exit codes are handled during recursive directory traversal. When `search_file` returns 2 for an unreadable file inside a directory tree, that should make the overall exit code 2, but the logic at lines 247-260 only updates `exit_code` based on result values without properly tracking errors.
